# Cookies: a run keeps one cookie jar. /cookies/set sets a cookie and
# redirects to /cookies, which lists the cookies it received; the next
# request gets the cookie too. Run with --no-cookies to see them fail.

### Set a cookie
GET {{baseUrl}}/cookies/set?session=abc123

> {% test("cookie set", () => expect(res.json().cookies).toEqual({session: "abc123"})) %}

### Sent on later requests
GET {{baseUrl}}/cookies

> {% test("cookie sent", () => expect(res.json().cookies.session).toBe("abc123")) %}
